[1m[38;5;231mWhat establishes the user's identity for tracking?[0m

[38;5;153m❯[39m [38;5;246m1.[39m [38;5;153mAuth API assigns it (Recommended)[39m
     [38;5;246mlogin() POSTs to API_ENDPOINT and the server returns a real userId. Only option where the ID genuinely means 'this
[39m     [38;5;246mperson authenticated'. Requires a real endpoint or an agreed mock contract, and makes login() async.[39m
  [38;5;246m2.[39m Client-generated UUID
     [38;5;246mA UUID stored in localStorage. No backend required, works immediately. Identifies a browser rather than a person: [39m
     [38;5;246mresets on storage clear, splits across devices, shared by everyone on one machine. Costly to re-attribute later.[39m
  [38;5;246m3.[39m Use the username
     [38;5;246mTreat the username already passed to login() as the identity key. No new machinery at all. Breaks if usernames are
[39m     [38;5;246mmutable, and puts user-supplied data into your tracking store.[39m
